The doctor opens his door and calls my name.
"Frau Flores, please," he says.
I stand up slowly and walk into his consultation room.
"Good morning, Frau Flores," he greets me.
"Please take a seat."
I sit down on the chair next to his desk.
"How are you doing today?" he asks.
"I do not feel good at all," I answer honestly.
"Where does it hurt then?" the doctor asks me.
I point to my head.
"My head hurts," I explain.
Then I point to my throat and to my chest.
"My throat and my chest hurt too."
I breathe in deeply and cough a little.
The doctor nods and writes something down.
I have one more question.
I ask him without much hope.
"Can I play badminton tomorrow evening?"
I really want to play, because it is always a lot of fun.
The doctor stops writing and looks at me surprised.
